"{\n  \"entities\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Body Language\",\n      \"type\": \"Communication Method\",\n      \"description\": \"Body language is a form of nonverbal communication that involves the use of physical behaviors, expressions, and movements to convey information, emotions, and intentions. It plays a crucial role in social interactions and relationships, often without the conscious awareness of the individuals involved.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Purpose\": \"Convey emotions, intentions, and social cues\",\n        \"Common Usage\": \"Daily basis, often unconsciously\",\n        \"Impact on Communication\": \"Significant, estimated to make up 55% of communication\",\n        \"Versatility\": \"Used in various settings including professional, social, and romantic\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"emotions\",\n      \"type\": \"Concept\",\n      \"description\": \"Emotions are complex psychological states that involve subjective feelings, physiological responses, and expressive behaviors. They play a significant role in human communication and social interactions, often conveyed and interpreted through body language and proxemics.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Nature\": \"Psychological and physiological state\",\n        \"Role in Communication\": \"Conveyed and interpreted through body language and proxemics\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"crossing one\\\"s arms\",\n      \"type\": \"Body Language Gesture\",\n      \"description\": \"Crossing one\\\"s arms is a non-verbal communication gesture that can signal defensiveness or discomfort.\",\n      \"attributes\": {\n        \"Common Interpretation\": \"Defensiveness or discomfort\",\n        \"Usage Context\": \"Social and professional interactions\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"mirroring gestures\",\n      \"type\": \"Body Language\",\n      \"description\": \"Mirroring gestures is a form of body language where individuals unconsciously mimic 